# WRL Documentation

> Developer documentation for Web Resource Ledger (WRL) — a cryptographic web evidence API. Captures web pages with Ed25519 signatures, RFC 3161 timestamps, and optional eIDAS-qualified timestamps. Produces signed WACZ bundles.

## Docs

- [Getting Started](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/): Quickstart guide — first capture in five minutes
- [Authentication](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/authentication/): API key management and OAuth login
- [Verification](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/verification/): How to verify capture authenticity
- [Legal Evidence](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/legal-evidence/): FRE 901/902, eIDAS Art. 41(2) legal framework
- [Batch Captures](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/batch/): Bulk capture API for multiple URLs
- [Schedules](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/schedules/): Recurring scheduled captures via cron triggers
- [Limits & Quotas](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/limits/): Rate limits and usage quotas
- [Webhooks](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/webhooks/): Event notifications for capture completion
- [MCP Server](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/mcp/): Model Context Protocol integration for AI agents
- [API Reference](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/api-reference/): Full REST API specification
- [Architecture](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/architecture/): System design and data flow
- [Compare](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/compare/): Comparison with other web archiving tools
- [Security & Compliance](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/security/): Security practices, GDPR, and compliance artifacts
- [Security Whitepaper](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/security/whitepaper/): Architecture, trust model, and security controls
- [Data Processing Agreement](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/security/dpa/): GDPR Article 28 DPA template for enterprise customers
- [Subprocessors](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/security/subprocessors/): Third-party services that process data on behalf of WRL
- [Incident Response](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/security/incident-response/): How WRL detects and responds to security incidents
- [Data Retention](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/security/data-retention/): Data retention periods and deletion policy
- [SWGDE Alignment](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/security/swgde-compliance/): SWGDE 21-F-001 v1.1 alignment mapping for forensic web capture
- [Support](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/support/): Where to ask for help, what to include, and that no plan includes an SLA
- [How WRL Was Built](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/about/): Development history, with the prompts, decisions and outcomes of each phase

## Use cases

- [Preserve a Website Before It Goes Offline](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/use-cases/preserve-a-site/): Capture every page of a site from its sitemap, with a verification link for each page
- [Capture Evidence of a Seller or Listing](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/use-cases/marketplace-evidence/): Timestamped evidence of a listing, seller profile or review, optionally with an eIDAS qualified timestamp
- [Document a Compliance Survey Across Many Websites](https://docs.webresourceledger.com/use-cases/compliance-survey/): The same kind of page across many organisations, each with a verifiable record

